ment `count`.\\n     - Update `a, b = b, next_fib`.\\n\\n5. **Return the Result**\\n   - Return the `n`-th element from the `fibonacci` list.\\n\\n6. **Edge Cases**\\n   - Handle invalid inputs as specified.\\n   - For `n > 20`, return an appropriate error message or handle as specified.\\n\\n7. **Primality Check**\\n   - Implement a primality check function with complexity O(sqrt(fibonacci_number)).\\n\\n8. **Complexity**\\n   - Ensure the overall complexity is O(n * sqrt(fibonacci_number)).\\n\\n9. **Test Cases**\\n   - Verify the function with the provided test cases:\\n     - `prime_fib(1) == 2`\\n     - `prime_fib(2) == 3`\\n     - `prime_fib(3) == 5`\\n     - `prime_fib(4) == 13`\\n     - `prime_fib(5) == 89`\\n\\n10. **Documentation**\\n    - Ensure the docstring matches the original specification."}'}]
